Andy Johnson <usenet@REMOVETHIS.swervy.tk> writes:
> Do you still get experience in a weapon if you only throw it? It seems
> obvious for arrows, darts, etc, but does it work the same for ALL
> types?
> 
> It seems to be taking me FOREVER to advance in Hammer with my
> Mjollnir. I always throw if they're not already next to me, and so I
> only rarely use it in melee (and yes, I've been hit by it a few
> times. I still think it's safer).
> 
> Does the weapon have to be designated a 'throwing' weapon to get the
> experience for being thrown?

In general, no. Throwing ammo without a launcher (bow/sling), or
throwing a launcher itself, won't exercise the relevant skill;
throwing other weapons will. The only place that the throwing weapon
distinction matters is for to-hit bonuses and penalties when throwing,
autoquivering, and whether a cursed weapon will slip. Of course, you
have to be able to hit the monster effectively to get the exercise
credit...

(If it seems to be taking longer than you'd expect, you might want to
check that you actually have a slot open.)

